  "description": "AZUFOQ crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C80 H92 Br8 Cl4 O50 Tb10 2+,2(Cl1 1-),2(C1 H4 O1). From the CIF bond table, Tb1 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb2 (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb3 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb4 (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb5 (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb1A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb4A (Tb) has 8 O neighbors; Tb2A (Tb) has 9 O neighbors; Tb3A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors; Tb5A (Tb) has 7 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 17 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.656-4.028 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 94.69-113.06°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Tb10L6L'2(OH)8(OAc)6Cl4(CH3OH)2(H2O)2]·2Cl·2CH3OH. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 8 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 6 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
